    "roles": ["touring", "band_member", "session", "bandleader", "educator"],
    "summary": "James Brown's drummer from 1965 to about 1970, in tandem with Jabo Starks. Played softly, with ghost notes felt more than heard, a kick that rarely lands where you expect and a backbeat that moves. His unaccompanied break on 'Funky Drummer' is among the most sampled recordings ever made, yet he received almost no credit or royalties for it. Spent his later decades as a much-loved bandleader in Madison, Wisconsin."
  },
